{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>YHWH shall strike you with consumption.</b> He mentioned the special Name and did not say 'Elohim shall strike you'; and this is the attribute of justice in this place. Similar to it (Genesis 6:7): ״ויאמר ה' אמחה״, (Exodus 14:14): ״ה' ילחם לכם״ — which is the attribute of justice. For thus we find the name Elohim to be the attribute of mercy in many places, as in (Genesis 8:1): ״ויזכור אלהים את נח״, (ibid. 20): ״וירפא אלהים את אבימלך״, for each of the attributes is included within the other. And because of this, He said יככה with the additional ה to indicate the attribute of justice that disciplines a person — as it is written (Leviticus 26:18): ״ולהספתי ליסרה אתכם שבע״, with the additional ה called שבע, and He disciplines with seven scourges. And so He mentioned here seven illnesses: consumption, fever, and all the rest."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:39.050403833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}